LIB_LOAD("ry",{"ry1":{"challenge":[{"q":"What was J. C. Ryle's favourite sport?","o":["Cricket","Swimming","Golf","Football"],"why":"He played for Oxford."},{"q":"Which verse helped change Ryle's life?","o":["Ephesians 2:8","Genesis 1:1","Psalm 23:1","John 11:35"],"why":"By grace are ye saved."},{"q":"What happened to the Ryle family bank?","o":["It collapsed","It doubled","It was sold","It became a church"],"why":"They lost almost everything."},{"q":"What city did Ryle become the first bishop of?","o":["Liverpool","Lagos","London","Oxford"],"why":"In 1880."},{"q":"James 4:14 says your life is like...?","o":["A vapour","A mountain","A wall","An ocean"],"why":"It appears for a little time."},{"q":"What did Tobi say he'd do 'later'?","o":["Think about God","Play cricket","Eat","Go to school"],"why":"Ryle said: start now."},{"q":"What was hard to bend?","o":["The old iroko tree","The young sapling","A feather","A rope"],"why":"Like hardened habits."},{"q":"\"It is good for a man that he bear the yoke in his...\"","o":["youth","old age","sleep","house"],"why":"Lamentations 3:27."},{"q":"Who did John write to 'because ye are strong'?","o":["Young men","Old men","Kings","Fishermen"],"why":"1 John 2:14."},{"q":"What did Ryle say to give your youth to?","o":["Jesus","The devil","Money","Fame"],"why":"It's too valuable to waste."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! What does 'Ìwà rere lẹ̀ṣọ́ ènìyàn' mean?","o":["Good character is a person's true beauty","Money is power","Sleep is good","Be quick"],"why":"A Yoruba proverb."},"choices":[{"title":"Later, not now","q":"A friend says, \"Church and God are for old people. We'll get serious later.\"","o":[{"t":"Say kindly that you want to follow God now, while you're young.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Remember thy Creator in the days of thy youth."},{"t":"Agree and put God off.","f":"Nobody is promised tomorrow, and the best years are now."},{"t":"Laugh at your friend.","f":"Be honest, but be kind."}]},{"title":"A small lie","q":"You've started telling small lies to get out of chores. It's becoming easy.","o":[{"t":"Stop now, while the habit is still young and bendable.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Bend the sapling before it becomes an iroko."},{"t":"Keep going. It's only small.","f":"Small habits harden into big ones."},{"t":"Stop when you're an adult.","f":"By then it'll be much harder."}]},{"title":"Too young to help?","q":"Your church needs volunteers for a children's outreach, but you think, \"I'm just a teenager.\"","o":[{"t":"Volunteer. God uses young people now.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Let no man despise thy youth."},{"t":"Leave it to the adults.","f":"You're strong, and God can use you today."},{"t":"Wait until you're older.","f":"David, Joseph and Daniel didn't wait."}]},{"title":"Proud of your gifts","q":"You're top of the class and captain of the team. You feel like you don't need God.","o":[{"t":"Thank God for your gifts and remember that only His grace saves.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Ryle had it all too, and found it wasn't enough."},{"t":"Rely on your talent alone.","f":"Talent fades; grace lasts."},{"t":"Look down on others.","f":"That's pride, the first danger in the next chapter!"}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"cricketfield","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 1 of Thoughts for Young Men in real life."},{"sc":"church","n":"🏏 Talents are great, but only God's grace saves."},{"sc":"dawn","n":"🌫️ Life is short. Don't say 'later' to God."},{"sc":"trees","n":"🌳 Build good habits now, while you're still bendable."},{"sc":"cricketfield","n":"💪 You're young and strong. God can use you today!"}],"stops":{"ry1s1":{"story":[{"sc":"cricketfield","n":"In 1816, a baby boy was born into a rich family in England. His name was John Charles Ryle, but everyone came to know him as {J. C. Ryle}."},{"sc":"cricketfield","n":"He went to {Eton} and then to Oxford University. He was clever, he won prizes, and he was a star cricketer who played for Oxford."},{"sc":"cricketfield","w":"ryle","e":"smirk","t":"I was strong, popular and sure of myself. I thought I had my whole life worked out. God was not part of the plan."},{"sc":"church","n":"But when he was about twenty-one, Ryle became seriously ill. Lying in bed, he began to read the Bible and pray. Things he'd ignored for years suddenly mattered."},{"sc":"church","n":"The story is told that one Sunday he walked into a church just as the Bible was being read, slowly and clearly: 'By {grace} are ye saved through faith.' The words went straight to his heart."},{"sc":"church","w":"ryle","e":"big","t":"Saved by grace! Not by my cleverness, not by my cricket, not by my good name. A gift from God, through Jesus Christ. I believed it, and everything changed."},{"sc":"town","n":"A few years later, his father's bank collapsed and the family lost almost everything. Ryle had once hoped for a career in politics. Instead, he became a minister of the gospel."},{"sc":"study","n":"He became famous for writing short, plain books and {tract}s that anyone could understand. In 1880 he became the first Bishop of Liverpool. And he never forgot what it was like to be young."},{"sc":"study","w":"ryle","e":"smile","t":"So I wrote a little book just for young people. I'm going to be honest with you, because I care about you. Will you listen?"}],"quote":{"text":"For by grace are ye saved through faith; and that not of yourselves: it is the gift of God: not of works, lest any man should boast.","who":"Ephesians 2:8-9","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Everything can change","text":"Ryle had everything: brains, sport, money and popularity. But it was God's grace, not his gifts, that changed his life. He wrote to young people because he remembered how easy it is to think you've got it all worked out."},"think":"Ryle was a star at sport and school, but he said none of that could save him. What are you tempted to trust in instead of God?","quiz":[{"q":"What sport was J. C. Ryle a star at?","o":["Cricket","Football","Boxing","Tennis"],"why":"He played cricket for Oxford University."},{"q":"What happened when Ryle was about twenty-one?","o":["He became seriously ill and began to read the Bible","He became a bishop","He moved to Nigeria","He won the lottery"],"why":"Illness made him think about God."},{"q":"Which verse touched his heart?","o":["\"By grace are ye saved through faith\"","\"Go to the ant\"","\"Jesus wept\"","\"In the beginning\""],"why":"Ephesians 2:8."},{"q":"What happened to his father's bank?","o":["It collapsed, and the family lost almost everything","It became huge","It moved to London","Ryle ran it"],"why":"And Ryle became a minister instead of a politician."},{"q":"What did Ryle become in 1880?","o":["The first Bishop of Liverpool","A cricket captain","Prime Minister","A banker"],"why":"He wrote plain books that anyone could understand."}]},"ry1s2":{"story":[{"sc":"college","w":"rytobi","e":"smile","t":"God? I'll think about Him later. When I'm old. Maybe at forty. Right now I just want to enjoy life!"},{"sc":"college","w":"ryle","e":"worried","t":"Tobi, that's exactly what I used to think. 'Plenty of time.' But here's the hard truth: nobody has promised you tomorrow."},{"sc":"dawn","n":"Ryle reminded young people of something we don't like to think about. Some people live to be very old. Some don't. Life is precious, and it is not ours to control."},{"sc":"dawn","w":"ryle","e":"smile","t":"The Bible says your life is like a vapour, like the mist you see over the field in the morning. Beautiful, but it doesn't stay long."},{"sc":"dawn","w":"rytobi","e":"worried","t":"That's a bit scary."},{"sc":"dawn","w":"ryle","e":"smile","t":"It doesn't have to be scary! It's an invitation. If life is short, then don't waste the best part of it. Give it to God now, while you're young and strong, and enjoy every day with Him."},{"sc":"valleysun","w":"ryada","e":"big","t":"So 'later' could be too late, but 'now' is always the right time!"},{"sc":"valleysun","w":"ryle","e":"big","t":"Exactly, Ada. Don't wait to be old to be wise."}],"quote":{"text":"Remember now thy Creator in the days of thy youth, while the evil days come not.","who":"Ecclesiastes 12:1","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Don't say 'later'","text":"Ryle saw many young people plan to turn to God 'later'. But no one is promised tomorrow. That's not a reason to be afraid. It's a reason to start now, and to enjoy life with God from the beginning."},"think":"What's something good you've been putting off 'until later'? Why not start it today?","quiz":[{"q":"When did Tobi plan to think about God?","o":["Later, when he was old","Today","Never","Every morning"],"why":"\"Maybe at forty.\""},{"q":"What does James 4:14 compare life to?","o":["A vapour or mist","A rock","A river","A mountain"],"why":"It appears for a little time."},{"q":"What did Ryle say about tomorrow?","o":["Nobody has promised it to you","It's guaranteed","It doesn't matter","It's always better"],"why":"So start now."},{"q":"Did Ryle want Tobi to be afraid?","o":["No, he wanted it to be an invitation to start now","Yes, very afraid","He didn't care","He wanted him to give up"],"why":"Enjoy every day with God."},{"q":"Ecclesiastes 12:1 says to remember your Creator when?","o":["In the days of thy youth","When you're old","Only on Sundays","When you're in trouble"],"why":"Now!"}]},"ry1s3":{"story":[{"sc":"trees","w":"ryle","e":"smile","t":"Tobi, try bending this young sapling."},{"sc":"trees","w":"rytobi","e":"smile","t":"Easy! Look, it bends right over."},{"sc":"trees","w":"ryle","e":"smirk","t":"Now try bending that big old iroko tree."},{"sc":"trees","w":"rytobi","e":"shock","t":"Ha! Impossible. It's as hard as iron."},{"sc":"trees","w":"ryle","e":"big","t":"That's what habits are like. While you're young, you can bend them any way you want. But every day, they grow a little harder. By the time you're old, they're like that iroko: very hard to move."},{"sc":"trees","n":"Ryle warned that bad habits started in youth, like lying, laziness or a bad temper, are much harder to break later. But good habits started young, like prayer, honesty and hard work, grow strong and stay."},{"sc":"trees","w":"ryada","e":"smile","t":"So the habits I'm building now are the person I'll be at forty!"},{"sc":"trees","w":"ryle","e":"smile","t":"Yes! You're not just a teenager. You're a tree that's still growing. Grow in the right direction."}],"quote":{"text":"Train up a child in the way he should go: and when he is old, he will not depart from it.","who":"Proverbs 22:6","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Bend while you can","text":"A young tree bends easily; an old one won't move. Habits are the same. The habits you build as a teenager, good or bad, become the shape of your life. Now is the easiest time to grow straight."},"think":"Name one good habit you want to start this week, and one bad habit you want to stop before it hardens.","proverb":{"text":"Ìwà rere lẹ̀ṣọ́ ènìyàn.","lang":"Yoruba","mean":"Good character is a person's true beauty. It's what people remember about you."},"quiz":[{"q":"What was easy for Tobi to bend?","o":["A young sapling","An old iroko tree","An iron bar","A rock"],"why":"Young things bend easily."},{"q":"What did Ryle compare the old iroko tree to?","o":["Old, hardened habits","A good friend","A church","A cricket bat"],"why":"Very hard to move."},{"q":"Which bad habits did Ryle warn about?","o":["Lying, laziness and a bad temper","Praying","Honesty","Hard work"],"why":"They're harder to break later."},{"q":"What does Lamentations 3:27 say is good to do in your youth?","o":["Bear the yoke","Do nothing","Sleep a lot","Avoid work"],"why":"Learn discipline young."},{"q":"What does the Yoruba proverb say good character is?","o":["A person's true beauty","Useless","Only for old people","Boring"],"why":"Ìwà rere lẹ̀ṣọ́ ènìyàn."}]},"ry1s4":{"story":[{"sc":"cricketfield","w":"rycoach","e":"big","t":"Come on, team! Faster! Stronger! You've got young legs. Use them!"},{"sc":"cricketfield","n":"Tobi and Ada were at sports practice. Everyone was full of energy."},{"sc":"cricketfield","w":"ryle","e":"smile","t":"Look at all that strength! When I was young, I loved sport just like you. And do you know what? God loves your energy too."},{"sc":"cricketfield","w":"ryle","e":"big","t":"The apostle John wrote a letter to young men, and he said: I write to you because you are strong. Young people aren't just the church of tomorrow. You are useful to God today!"},{"sc":"cricketfield","w":"ryada","e":"worried","t":"But what can a teenager do for God?"},{"sc":"cricketfield","w":"ryle","e":"smile","t":"David fought Goliath as a youth. Joseph was a teenager when his story began. Daniel stood firm in Babylon as a young man. And Timothy was told: let no man despise thy youth."},{"sc":"cricketfield","w":"ryle","e":"big","t":"The devil wants your youth, because he knows how much it's worth. So don't give it to him. Give it to Jesus."},{"sc":"cricketfield","w":"rytobi","e":"big","t":"Young and strong, for God. I like that."}],"quote":{"text":"Let no man despise thy youth; but be thou an example of the believers, in word, in conversation, in charity, in spirit, in faith, in purity.","who":"1 Timothy 4:12","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Your strength is for God","text":"John wrote to young men because they were strong. Your energy, your courage and your fresh ideas are gifts. Ryle said the devil wants your youth because it's so valuable. Give it to Jesus instead."},"think":"What strengths and energy do you have right now that God could use?","quiz":[{"q":"Why did John write to young men?","o":["Because they were strong","Because they were weak","Because they were rich","Because they were lazy"],"why":"1 John 2:14."},{"q":"Which Bible hero fought Goliath as a youth?","o":["David","Moses","Paul","Noah"],"why":"Young and strong for God."},{"q":"Who was told 'Let no man despise thy youth'?","o":["Timothy","Peter","Jonah","Saul"],"why":"1 Timothy 4:12."},{"q":"Why did Ryle say the devil wants your youth?","o":["Because it is so valuable","Because it's useless","He doesn't","Because he's bored"],"why":"So give it to Jesus."},{"q":"According to 1 John 2:14, what abides in strong young people?","o":["The word of God","Fear","Money","Pride"],"why":"And they overcome the wicked one."}]}}},"ry2":{"challenge":[{"q":"What was Ryle's first danger?","o":["Pride","Rain","Cricket","School"],"why":"It whispers 'You don't need anyone.'"},{"q":"\"Pride goeth before...\"","o":["destruction","dinner","Sunday","success"],"why":"Proverbs 16:18."},{"q":"What did Ada lose because of pride?","o":["Her next competition","Her phone","Her shoes","Her house"],"why":"She stopped preparing and listening."},{"q":"What was the second danger?","o":["Loving pleasure too much","Loving God","Loving your family","Reading"],"why":"Fun is a gift, not a master."},{"q":"2 Timothy 3:4 warns about lovers of pleasures more than lovers of...?","o":["God","money","sport","food"],"why":"Keep God first."},{"q":"What was the third danger?","o":["Thoughtlessness","Thinking too much","Studying","Sleeping"],"why":"Not asking where things lead."},{"q":"What does Haggai 1:5 say?","o":["Consider your ways","Hurry up","Don't think","Sleep more"],"why":"Stop and think."},{"q":"What was the fourth danger?","o":["The fear of man","The fear of the dark","The fear of dogs","The fear of exams"],"why":"Worrying what people think."},{"q":"Who denied Jesus three times?","o":["Peter","John","Paul","Timothy"],"why":"But Jesus forgave him."},{"q":"What does trusting in the Lord make you, according to Proverbs 29:25?","o":["Safe","Rich","Famous","Tired"],"why":"The fear of man is a snare."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! What does the Hausa proverb call pride?","o":["The turban of misfortune","A crown of gold","A good friend","A sweet cake"],"why":"Girman kai rawanin tsiya."},"choices":[{"title":"Know-it-all","q":"Your teacher corrects a mistake in your project. You feel annoyed because you're usually the best.","o":[{"t":"Thank her and learn from it.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! A humble heart is teachable."},{"t":"Argue that you were right.","f":"Pride stops you learning."},{"t":"Ignore the correction.","f":"God gives grace to the humble."}]},{"title":"One more episode","q":"It's 11pm. You have an exam tomorrow and you're on your fourth episode of a show.","o":[{"t":"Switch it off and sleep.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Fun is a gift, not a master."},{"t":"Watch just two more.","f":"That's how pleasure takes over."},{"t":"Stay up all night.","f":"It feels good now and costs you later."}]},{"title":"Forward it?","q":"Someone sends an embarrassing photo of a classmate to your group chat.","o":[{"t":"Don't share it, and say it's not kind.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Consider your ways: who will this hurt?"},{"t":"Share it. Everyone else is.","f":"The crowd often drifts the wrong way."},{"t":"React with a laughing emoji.","f":"Even that adds to someone's hurt."}]},{"title":"Laughed at","q":"Someone mocks you for going to a church youth camp.","o":[{"t":"Stay calm and kind, and don't hide your faith.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! People's laughter lasts a moment; God's approval lasts forever."},{"t":"Say you were forced to go.","f":"That's the fear of man, like Peter by the fire."},{"t":"Mock them back.","f":"Be brave, but be kind too."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"college","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 2 of Thoughts for Young Men in real life."},{"sc":"college","n":"🦚 Stay humble and teachable."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"🎮 Keep fun in its place: God first, work next, then play."},{"sc":"college","n":"🤔 Stop and think before you act, post or share."},{"sc":"pentecost","n":"🦁 Don't fear people's laughter. Be bold, like Peter."}],"stops":{"ry2s1":{"story":[{"sc":"college","w":"ryle","e":"stern","t":"I've seen many young people ruined. Not all at once, but step by step. So let me warn you about the dangers ahead, like a guide pointing out holes in the road."},{"sc":"college","w":"ryle","e":"stern","t":"The first danger is {pride}."},{"sc":"college","n":"Ada had just won the inter-school debate competition. Everyone was congratulating her. At first she was thankful. But slowly, something changed."},{"sc":"college","w":"ryada","e":"smirk","t":"Honestly, the rest of my class are just slow. I don't need the teacher's advice anymore. I already know more than her."},{"sc":"college","w":"rykemi","e":"worried","t":"Ada, you've changed. You don't listen to anyone now."},{"sc":"college","w":"ryle","e":"worried","t":"Pride is sneaky. It whispers: 'You're better than them. You don't need help. You don't even need God.' And a person who thinks they know everything stops learning."},{"sc":"college","w":"ryle","e":"smile","t":"Young people especially are tempted to think they know better than everyone older. Some of the time, you might! But a humble heart is teachable, and a teachable person keeps growing."},{"sc":"college","n":"Ada lost her next competition badly, because she hadn't prepared or listened to advice. She went to her teacher and to Kemi and said sorry. 'I let it go to my head,' she admitted."}],"quote":{"text":"God resisteth the proud, but giveth grace unto the humble.","who":"James 4:6","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Stay teachable","text":"Ryle's first danger is pride: thinking you're better than others or don't need God. Pride stops you learning and pushes people away. Be thankful for your gifts, and stay humble and teachable."},"think":"When did you last let someone correct you or give you advice? How did you respond?","proverb":{"text":"Girman kai rawanin tsiya.","lang":"Hausa","mean":"Pride is the turban of misfortune. Wear pride on your head, and trouble isn't far behind."},"quiz":[{"q":"What was the first danger Ryle warned about?","o":["Pride","Laziness","Money","Sport"],"why":"A sneaky danger."},{"q":"What did Ada win?","o":["An inter-school debate competition","A cricket match","A lottery","A singing contest"],"why":"Then pride crept in."},{"q":"What does pride stop you doing?","o":["Learning","Eating","Sleeping","Talking"],"why":"A know-it-all stops growing."},{"q":"What does James 4:6 say God gives the humble?","o":["Grace","Money","Trouble","Nothing"],"why":"But He resists the proud."},{"q":"What does Proverbs 16:18 say goes before destruction?","o":["Pride","Humility","Wisdom","Kindness"],"why":"And a haughty spirit before a fall."}]},"ry2s2":{"story":[{"sc":"townnight","n":"Tobi had a new game. He played after school. He played after dinner. He played under his blanket at 2am."},{"sc":"townnight","w":"rytobi","e":"big","t":"Just one more level!"},{"sc":"college","n":"Next morning, he was too tired to concentrate. He hadn't done his homework. He'd skipped his chores. He forgot to call his grandmother on her birthday."},{"sc":"college","w":"ryle","e":"smile","t":"Now, Tobi, I'm not against fun! I loved cricket. God made laughter, games and good times. They're gifts."},{"sc":"college","w":"ryle","e":"stern","t":"But the second danger is loving pleasure too much: living only for the next good feeling. Some pleasures are wrong in themselves. Others are fine, but they grow until they push out everything important."},{"sc":"college","w":"ryle","e":"worried","t":"In my day, it was drinking, gambling and wild parties that ruined young men. In your day, there are new ones. But the trap is the same: it feels good now, and it costs you later."},{"sc":"college","w":"rytobi","e":"worried","t":"So I have to stop gaming forever?"},{"sc":"college","w":"ryle","e":"smile","t":"No! Put it in its place. Work first, then play. God first, then everything else. Then fun stays a gift instead of becoming a master."}],"quote":{"text":"All things are lawful unto me, but all things are not expedient: all things are lawful for me, but I will not be brought under the power of any.","who":"1 Corinthians 6:12","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Fun is a gift, not a master","text":"Ryle wasn't against fun. But he warned about loving pleasure more than God, when the next good feeling becomes the most important thing. Keep fun in its place: God first, work next, then enjoy the play."},"think":"Is there anything fun in your life that's starting to push out more important things?","quiz":[{"q":"Why was Tobi tired in the morning?","o":["He played games until 2am","He was ill","He ran a race","He was praying"],"why":"\"Just one more level!\""},{"q":"Was Ryle against all fun?","o":["No, he said God made fun and good times","Yes, completely","He never mentioned it","He hated cricket"],"why":"Fun is a gift."},{"q":"What was the second danger?","o":["Loving pleasure too much","Loving God","Working hard","Reading"],"why":"Living only for good feelings."},{"q":"What order did Ryle suggest?","o":["God first, work next, then play","Play first, then nothing","Only work","Only play"],"why":"Then fun stays a gift."},{"q":"What does 1 Corinthians 6:12 say Paul won't be brought under?","o":["The power of any thing","The rain","A king","A teacher"],"why":"Don't let anything master you."}]},"ry2s3":{"story":[{"sc":"college","w":"rykemi","e":"smirk","t":"Ha! Look at this funny video of Bisi falling over in the hall. Share it to the class group!"},{"sc":"college","w":"rytobi","e":"smile","t":"Sure, why not."},{"sc":"college","n":"Tobi pressed 'send' without a second thought. By lunchtime, the whole school had seen it. Bisi cried in the toilets all afternoon."},{"sc":"college","w":"rytobi","e":"worried","t":"I didn't mean to hurt her. I just... didn't think."},{"sc":"college","w":"ryle","e":"smile","t":"That's the third danger, Tobi: thoughtlessness. Not stopping to ask, 'Where will this lead? Who will this hurt? What would God think?'"},{"sc":"college","w":"ryle","e":"stern","t":"Many young people don't mean to do wrong. They just don't think. They drift along with the crowd, and the crowd often drifts the wrong way. Some even laugh at faith without ever thinking about it seriously."},{"sc":"college","w":"ryle","e":"smile","t":"God says: consider your ways. Stop, think, then act. It takes two seconds, and it can save you years of regret."},{"sc":"college","n":"Tobi deleted the video, asked others to delete it too, and went to say sorry to Bisi. It was hard. But it was right."}],"quote":{"text":"Ponder the path of thy feet, and let all thy ways be established.","who":"Proverbs 4:26","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Stop and think","text":"Ryle's third danger is thoughtlessness: drifting along without asking where your choices lead. Most harm isn't planned; it just isn't thought about. Before you act, ask: who will this hurt, and what would God think?"},"think":"Before you post, share or say something this week, try the two-second 'consider your ways' pause.","quiz":[{"q":"What did Tobi share without thinking?","o":["A video of Bisi falling over","A Bible verse","His homework","A birthday card"],"why":"The whole school saw it."},{"q":"What was the third danger?","o":["Thoughtlessness","Hard work","Prayer","Kindness"],"why":"Not stopping to think."},{"q":"What three questions did Ryle suggest?","o":["Where will this lead? Who will it hurt? What would God think?","How much? When? Why not?","Who's watching? Will I be caught? Is it fun?","None"],"why":"Stop, think, then act."},{"q":"What did Tobi do to put it right?","o":["Deleted the video and said sorry to Bisi","Shared it again","Blamed Kemi","Did nothing"],"why":"Hard, but right."},{"q":"What does Haggai 1:5 say?","o":["Consider your ways","Don't worry","Go faster","Never stop"],"why":"Think before you act."}]},"ry2s4":{"story":[{"sc":"college","n":"It was lunchtime. Ada usually closed her eyes and thanked God before eating. But today she was sitting with the popular girls."},{"sc":"college","w":"ryada","e":"worried","t":"If I pray, they'll laugh at me. Maybe I'll skip it, just this once..."},{"sc":"college","w":"ryle","e":"smile","t":"Ah, Ada. The fourth danger: {the fear of man}. I'm convinced that 'What will my friends say?' has kept more young people from following Jesus than almost anything else."},{"sc":"lastsupper","w":"ryjesus","e":"smile","t":"Simon, Simon... I have prayed for thee, that thy faith fail not: and when thou art converted, strengthen thy brethren."},{"sc":"courtyardfire","n":"Even Peter fell into this trap. The night Jesus was arrested, people by the fire said, 'You were with Jesus!' Peter was so afraid that he said he didn't know Him. Three times."},{"sc":"courtyardfire","w":"rypeter","e":"worried","t":"I know not the man!"},{"sc":"courtyardfire","n":"Then the Lord turned and looked at Peter. And Peter went out and wept bitterly."},{"sc":"pentecost","n":"But Jesus forgave Peter. A few weeks later, the same Peter stood up in front of thousands in Jerusalem and boldly told them about Jesus. The fear was gone."},{"sc":"college","w":"ryle","e":"big","t":"People's laughter lasts a moment. God's approval lasts forever. Be brave, Ada!"},{"sc":"college","n":"Ada bowed her head and prayed quietly. One of the girls asked her about it afterwards. It turned out she went to church too, and had been too scared to pray in public."}],"quote":{"text":"And the Lord turned, and looked upon Peter. And Peter remembered the word of the Lord... And Peter went out, and wept bitterly.","who":"Luke 22:61-62","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Don't fear their laughter","text":"Ryle said the fear of what people think stops more young people following Jesus than almost anything. Even Peter fell into it, but Jesus forgave him and made him bold. People's laughter lasts a moment; God's approval lasts forever."},"think":"Where are you most tempted to hide your faith? What could being brave look like there?","quiz":[{"q":"Why did Ada want to skip praying at lunch?","o":["She was afraid the popular girls would laugh","She wasn't hungry","She forgot","She was late"],"why":"The fear of man."},{"q":"What did Peter say when the servant girl recognised him?","o":["\"I know not the man\"","\"Yes, I'm His friend\"","\"Come and meet Him\"","Nothing"],"why":"Three times."},{"q":"What did Jesus do after Peter's denial?","o":["Turned and looked at Peter","Shouted at him","Ignored him forever","Ran away"],"why":"And Peter wept bitterly."},{"q":"What happened to Peter later?","o":["He boldly preached to thousands","He stayed scared forever","He left Jerusalem","He became a fisherman again forever"],"why":"Jesus forgave him and made him bold."},{"q":"Proverbs 29:25 says the fear of man brings a...?","o":["Snare","Reward","Party","Crown"],"why":"But trust in the Lord keeps you safe."}]}}},"ry3":{"challenge":[{"q":"What did a tiny crack do to the water pot?","o":["Let all the water out","Nothing","Made it stronger","Made it pretty"],"why":"So do 'little' sins."},{"q":"\"The wages of sin is...\"","o":["death","money","fun","sleep"],"why":"Romans 6:23."},{"q":"What is God's gift, according to Romans 6:23?","o":["Eternal life through Jesus","Gold","Fame","A big house"],"why":"Through Jesus Christ our Lord."},{"q":"Why did the rich young ruler go away sad?","o":["He had great possessions","Jesus was rude","He was hungry","He was lost"],"why":"He loved riches more."},{"q":"What did Ryle call his most important counsel?","o":["Get to know Jesus","Play more cricket","Be rich","Work alone"],"why":"Not just know about Him."},{"q":"What does Paul count as loss compared to knowing Christ?","o":["All things","Some things","Nothing","Only gold"],"why":"Philippians 3:8."},{"q":"What did Ada bring that Tobi didn't?","o":["A map","Food","A torch","A phone"],"why":"Feelings are not a map!"},{"q":"Which Psalm asks how a young man can cleanse his way?","o":["Psalm 119","Psalm 23","Psalm 1","Psalm 150"],"why":"Psalm 119:9."},{"q":"Who did Ryle say you become like?","o":["Your closest friends","Your enemies","Strangers","Nobody"],"why":"Choose friends wisely."},{"q":"\"He that walketh with wise men shall be...\"","o":["wise","rich","tired","lost"],"why":"Proverbs 13:20."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! According to 1 Corinthians 15:33, what do evil communications corrupt?","o":["Good manners","Good food","Good weather","Good books"],"why":"Be not deceived."},"choices":[{"title":"Just a small lie","q":"You told your parents a small lie about where you were. You think, \"It's tiny. It doesn't matter.\"","o":[{"t":"Tell them the truth and ask God to forgive you.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! No crack is too small to matter, and no sin too big for Jesus to forgive."},{"t":"Forget about it.","f":"Small cracks drain the pot."},{"t":"Tell another lie to cover it.","f":"Now the crack is bigger."}]},{"title":"One thing","q":"You love your phone so much that you skip prayer and church to keep scrolling.","o":[{"t":"Put Jesus first, even if it means less screen time.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Don't be like the rich young ruler. Jesus is worth more."},{"t":"Keep scrolling. God will understand.","f":"Don't let anything come between you and Jesus."},{"t":"Pray while scrolling.","f":"Give Him your full attention."}]},{"title":"No time to read","q":"You keep saying you're too busy to read the Bible.","o":[{"t":"Start small: one chapter a day at the same time.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Don't travel without a map."},{"t":"Wait for the holidays.","f":"You need a map for today's path."},{"t":"Just go by your feelings.","f":"Feelings are not a map!"}]},{"title":"The cool crowd","q":"A popular group wants you to join them, but they're always bullying younger students.","o":[{"t":"Stay friendly but don't join in, and choose friends who build you up.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! He that walketh with wise men shall be wise."},{"t":"Join them to be popular.","f":"You'll become like them."},{"t":"Join but stay quiet.","f":"Evil company corrupts good manners."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"kitchen","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 3 of Thoughts for Young Men in real life."},{"sc":"kitchen","n":"🏺 No sin is too small to matter, and none too big for Jesus to forgive."},{"sc":"road","n":"✝️ Don't just know about Jesus. Know Him and follow Him."},{"sc":"study","n":"📖 The Bible is your map. Read it daily and do what it says."},{"sc":"town","n":"👫 Choose close friends who pull you closer to God."}],"stops":{"ry3s1":{"story":[{"sc":"kitchen","w":"ryle","e":"smile","t":"So far I've warned you about dangers. Now let me give you some {counsel}: good advice to steer by. And the first is this: see sin for what it really is."},{"sc":"kitchen","w":"rytobi","e":"smirk","t":"Sin? I'm not a bad person. Just a few little things. A small lie here, a bit of cheating there. Everyone does it."},{"sc":"kitchen","n":"Tobi's mother had a big clay water pot in the kitchen. One day, Tobi noticed a tiny crack near the bottom. Just a hairline."},{"sc":"kitchen","w":"rytobi","e":"smile","t":"It's only a tiny crack. It doesn't matter."},{"sc":"kitchen","n":"But the next morning, the pot was empty and the kitchen floor was soaked. The tiny crack had let out every drop."},{"sc":"kitchen","w":"ryle","e":"stern","t":"That's what 'little' sins do, Tobi. They seem small, but they drain the life out of you. And they separate us from God. The Bible says the {wages} of sin is death."},{"sc":"kitchen","w":"ryle","e":"big","t":"But don't stop reading there! The same verse goes on: the gift of God is eternal life through Jesus Christ our Lord. You can't fix the crack yourself. But Jesus can make you new."},{"sc":"kitchen","w":"rytobi","e":"worried","t":"So the first step is to stop pretending sin is small... and then run to Jesus."}],"quote":{"text":"If we say that we have no sin, we deceive ourselves... If we confess our sins, he is faithful and just to forgive us our sins, and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness.","who":"1 John 1:8-9","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"No such thing as a 'little' sin","text":"Tobi thought his sins were small, like a hairline crack. But a tiny crack can empty a whole pot. Ryle said: see sin clearly. Then don't despair: run to Jesus, who forgives and makes us new."},"think":"Are there any 'little' sins you've been excusing? What would it mean to bring them to Jesus today?","quiz":[{"q":"What did Tobi say about his sins?","o":["They were only little things","They were huge","He had none","He was sorry"],"why":"\"Everyone does it.\""},{"q":"What happened to the pot with a tiny crack?","o":["All the water leaked out","Nothing","It got bigger","It was fixed"],"why":"A small crack drained every drop."},{"q":"What does Romans 6:23 say the wages of sin is?","o":["Death","Money","Fun","Nothing"],"why":"Sin pays badly."},{"q":"What is the gift of God?","o":["Eternal life through Jesus Christ","A new pot","Riches","Good grades"],"why":"The good news in the same verse."},{"q":"According to 1 John 1:9, what does God do if we confess?","o":["Forgives and cleanses us","Ignores us","Punishes us more","Nothing"],"why":"He is faithful and just."}]},"ry3s2":{"story":[{"sc":"road","w":"ryle","e":"smile","t":"My second piece of counsel is the most important of all: get to know the Lord Jesus Christ. Not just to know about Him, but to know Him."},{"sc":"road","n":"Once, a rich young man ran up to Jesus and knelt in front of Him. He was wealthy, important and well-behaved."},{"sc":"road","w":"ryruler","e":"worried","t":"Good Master, what shall I do that I may inherit eternal life?"},{"sc":"road","w":"ryjesus","e":"smile","t":"Thou knowest the commandments..."},{"sc":"road","w":"ryruler","e":"smile","t":"Master, all these have I observed from my youth."},{"sc":"road","n":"The Bible says that Jesus, beholding him, loved him."},{"sc":"road","w":"ryjesus","e":"smile","t":"One thing thou lackest: go thy way, sell whatsoever thou hast, and give to the poor, and thou shalt have treasure in heaven: and come, take up the cross, and follow me."},{"sc":"road","n":"The young man's face fell. He went away sad, because he had great possessions. He loved his riches more than he wanted Jesus."},{"sc":"road","w":"ryle","e":"worried","t":"He was so close! He was polite, religious and good. But he wouldn't let go of the one thing that stood between him and Jesus."},{"sc":"road","w":"ryle","e":"big","t":"Paul was different. He said he counted everything as loss compared to knowing Christ. Young people, Jesus is worth more than anything you could ever own. Make Him your friend now."}],"quote":{"text":"Then Jesus beholding him loved him, and said unto him, One thing thou lackest.","who":"Mark 10:21","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Jesus is worth everything","text":"The rich young ruler was good and religious, but loved his money more than Jesus, and went away sad. Ryle's biggest counsel: don't just know about Jesus. Know Him, follow Him, and let nothing come between you."},"think":"Is there anything in your life you'd find hard to let go of if Jesus asked you to?","quiz":[{"q":"What did the rich young man ask Jesus?","o":["What shall I do to inherit eternal life?","Where is the market?","Can I be king?","What's for dinner?"],"why":"Mark 10:17."},{"q":"How did Jesus feel about him?","o":["He loved him","He was angry","He didn't care","He laughed at him"],"why":"Jesus, beholding him, loved him."},{"q":"What did Jesus tell him to do?","o":["Sell what he had, give to the poor, and follow Him","Keep everything","Build a temple","Go home"],"why":"One thing thou lackest."},{"q":"Why did the young man go away sad?","o":["He had great possessions","He was ill","He was lost","He was tired"],"why":"He loved riches more."},{"q":"What did Paul count as loss compared to knowing Christ?","o":["All things","Nothing","Only money","Only food"],"why":"Philippians 3:8."}]},"ry3s3":{"story":[{"sc":"road","n":"Ada and Tobi went on a hike. Tobi was sure he knew the way. He didn't bring a map."},{"sc":"woods","w":"rytobi","e":"smile","t":"Trust me! It's left. No, right. No... hmm."},{"sc":"woods","n":"Two hours later, they were completely lost. Ada pulled out the trail map she'd packed. Twenty minutes later, they were back on the path."},{"sc":"woods","w":"ryada","e":"smirk","t":"Feelings are not a map, Tobi!"},{"sc":"study","w":"ryle","e":"smile","t":"Ha! Ada's right. My third counsel: make the Bible your map. Life is full of paths that look right but lead nowhere good. God's word shows you the way."},{"sc":"study","w":"ryle","e":"smile","t":"Read it every day, even if only a little. Read it with prayer. Ask God to help you understand it. And then, the most important part, do what it says."},{"sc":"study","w":"ryle","e":"big","t":"The Psalm asks: how can a young man keep his way clean? And the answer is: by living according to God's word."},{"sc":"study","w":"rytobi","e":"smile","t":"Okay. A chapter a day. Starting tonight. With a map, this time."}],"quote":{"text":"Thy word is a lamp unto my feet, and a light unto my path.","who":"Psalm 119:105","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Don't travel without a map","text":"Tobi got lost because he trusted his feelings instead of a map. Ryle says the Bible is God's map for life, especially for young people. Read it daily, read it with prayer, and do what it says."},"think":"What's one simple Bible-reading habit you could start, and stick to, this week?","quiz":[{"q":"Why did Tobi and Ada get lost?","o":["Tobi trusted his feelings instead of a map","It rained","Ada lost the map","They fell asleep"],"why":"\"Feelings are not a map!\""},{"q":"What did Ryle say is our map for life?","o":["The Bible","Our feelings","Social media","Our friends"],"why":"God's word shows the way."},{"q":"How did Ryle say to read the Bible?","o":["Every day, with prayer, and do what it says","Once a year","Only at church","Never"],"why":"Doing it is the most important part."},{"q":"According to Psalm 119:9, how can a young man cleanse his way?","o":["By taking heed according to God's word","By working harder","By being popular","By being rich"],"why":"God's word keeps us clean."},{"q":"Psalm 119:105 says God's word is a lamp to my...?","o":["Feet","House","Car","Phone"],"why":"And a light unto my path."}]},"ry3s4":{"story":[{"sc":"town","n":"Dayo was fun. He was the coolest boy in the estate. He also skipped school, cheated in tests, and was always in trouble."},{"sc":"town","w":"rydayo","e":"smirk","t":"Tobi, come with us tonight. We're going to the place your parents said you can't go. It's going to be wild!"},{"sc":"town","w":"rytobi","e":"worried","t":"Erm..."},{"sc":"town","w":"ryle","e":"stern","t":"Tobi, my fourth counsel is serious: be careful who your close friends are. You will become like the people you spend most time with."},{"sc":"town","w":"ryle","e":"smile","t":"I'm not saying be unkind to Dayo. Be friendly to everyone. Pray for him! But never make your closest friend someone who is not a friend of God. Friends pull you, either up or down."},{"sc":"town","w":"ryle","e":"big","t":"The Bible says: he that walketh with wise men shall be wise. Choose friends who make you better, braver and closer to God."},{"sc":"town","w":"rytobi","e":"smile","t":"No thanks, Dayo. But do you want to come to our youth football on Saturday instead?"},{"sc":"town","w":"rydayo","e":"shock","t":"...Football? Maybe. Okay."}],"quote":{"text":"Be not deceived: evil communications corrupt good manners.","who":"1 Corinthians 15:33","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Friends pull you up or down","text":"Ryle warned: you become like your closest friends. Be kind to everyone, but choose close friends who love God and make you better. And be the kind of friend who pulls others up."},"think":"Think about your three closest friends. Do they pull you closer to God or further away? Do you do that for them?","quiz":[{"q":"What did Dayo invite Tobi to do?","o":["Go somewhere his parents said he couldn't","Go to church","Do homework","Play football"],"why":"\"It's going to be wild!\""},{"q":"What did Ryle say you become like?","o":["The people you spend most time with","Your favourite film","Your teacher","Nobody"],"why":"Friends pull you up or down."},{"q":"Did Ryle tell Tobi to be unkind to Dayo?","o":["No, be friendly and pray for him","Yes","He said to fight him","He said to report him"],"why":"Kind to all, careful with close friends."},{"q":"What does Proverbs 13:20 say happens if you walk with wise men?","o":["You will be wise","You will be rich","You will be tired","You will be famous"],"why":"Choose wise friends."},{"q":"What did Tobi invite Dayo to?","o":["Youth football on Saturday","A party","The market","Nothing"],"why":"Pull others up!"}]}}},"ry4":{"challenge":[{"q":"What did Tobi wear in the race?","o":["A backpack","A crown","A cape","A hat"],"why":"A weight that slowed him down."},{"q":"When did Ryle say to break off known sin?","o":["At once","Slowly","Next month","When you're old"],"why":"Rule one."},{"q":"Hebrews 12:2 tells us to look unto...?","o":["Jesus","The crowd","The coach","The finish line"],"why":"The author and finisher of our faith."},{"q":"What was Ryle's second rule?","o":["Run from temptation","Sit next to it","Laugh at it","Ignore God"],"why":"Avoid it, pass not by it."},{"q":"What did Ryle compare temptation to?","o":["Hot puff-puff next to a hungry boy","A cold drink","A cricket ball","A book"],"why":"Asking for trouble!"},{"q":"Who said \"How can I sin against God?\"","o":["Joseph","Nehemiah","Peter","Tobi"],"why":"Genesis 39:9."},{"q":"\"The eyes of the LORD are in every...\"","o":["place","church","house","book"],"why":"Proverbs 15:3."},{"q":"Who prayed quickly before answering a king?","o":["Nehemiah","Joseph","Ryle","Dayo"],"why":"Nehemiah 2:4."},{"q":"Where did Jesus say to pray in Matthew 6:6?","o":["In your closet, with the door shut","On the street corner","Only in the temple","On a mountain only"],"why":"Pray to thy Father in secret."},{"q":"In what year did Ryle die?","o":["1900","1800","1950","2000"],"why":"At the age of 84."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! What does 2 Timothy 2:22 tell young people to follow?","o":["Righteousness, faith, charity and peace","Fame and money","The crowd","Their feelings"],"why":"Flee youthful lusts, follow righteousness."},"choices":[{"title":"Quit slowly?","q":"You know you've been using bad language. You plan to cut down \"a bit at a time\".","o":[{"t":"Stop now and ask God to help you.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Lay aside the weight. Don't run with the backpack."},{"t":"Cut down slowly over the year.","f":"A weight carried 'for now' slows the whole race."},{"t":"Keep going; everyone does it.","f":"Look unto Jesus, not the crowd."}]},{"title":"Late-night phone","q":"You keep seeing bad things on your phone late at night in your room.","o":[{"t":"Charge your phone outside your bedroom at night.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Don't just fight temptation. Run from it."},{"t":"Keep it there and try harder.","f":"Don't put puff-puff next to the hungry boy!"},{"t":"Hide it from your parents.","f":"Secrets make temptation stronger."}]},{"title":"Nobody's watching","q":"The shopkeeper gives you too much change. No one would ever know.","o":[{"t":"Give it back. God sees.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! The eyes of the LORD are in every place."},{"t":"Keep it. Their mistake.","f":"Joseph knew: it's against God, not just people."},{"t":"Keep half.","f":"Half-honest is still dishonest."}]},{"title":"Panic moment","q":"You're called to the front of the class to answer a hard question and your mind goes blank.","o":[{"t":"Send up a quick silent prayer, then do your best.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Pray anywhere, like Nehemiah."},{"t":"Freeze and panic.","f":"God is right there with you."},{"t":"Make something up to look clever.","f":"Honesty and a quick prayer work better."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"racetrack","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Thoughts for Young Men in real life."},{"sc":"racetrack","n":"🎒 Drop known sin at once. Don't run with the backpack."},{"sc":"college","n":"🏃 Run from temptation. Avoid what makes sin easy."},{"sc":"egyptcourt","n":"👁️ God sees everything, and He's a loving Father."},{"sc":"palace","n":"🙏 Pray in secret every day, and pray anywhere."}],"stops":{"ry4s1":{"story":[{"sc":"racetrack","w":"rycoach","e":"big","t":"On your marks! Get set!"},{"sc":"racetrack","w":"rycoach","e":"shock","t":"Wait, Tobi! Why are you wearing your school backpack in a race?"},{"sc":"racetrack","w":"rytobi","e":"smirk","t":"I'll take it off slowly, a bit at a time, while I run."},{"sc":"racetrack","n":"The race started. Tobi struggled and puffed, and came last by a mile."},{"sc":"racetrack","w":"ryle","e":"smile","t":"Now for some rules for life. Rule one: when you know something is a sin, break it off at once. Not slowly. Not 'next month'. Now."},{"sc":"racetrack","w":"ryle","e":"stern","t":"Many young people say, 'I'll stop gradually.' But a weight you carry 'for now' slows you down the whole race. The Bible says: lay aside every weight, and the sin which doth so easily {beset} us."},{"sc":"racetrack","w":"ryle","e":"big","t":"And you don't do it alone. Look unto Jesus, who ran the race before you and is cheering you on."},{"sc":"racetrack","n":"For the next race, Tobi threw the backpack off before the start. He didn't win, but he flew past half the runners."}],"quote":{"text":"Looking unto Jesus the author and finisher of our faith; who for the joy that was set before him endured the cross.","who":"Hebrews 12:2","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Drop it now","text":"Tobi tried to run with a backpack on, planning to take it off slowly. Ryle's first rule: when you know something is wrong, drop it at once. Lay aside the weight, look to Jesus, and run free."},"think":"Is there a habit you've been planning to stop 'gradually'? What would dropping it today look like?","quiz":[{"q":"What was Tobi wearing in the race?","o":["His school backpack","A crown","Boots","A coat"],"why":"And he came last!"},{"q":"What was Ryle's first rule?","o":["Break off known sin at once","Stop slowly","Never run","Wait until you're older"],"why":"Not slowly. Now."},{"q":"What does Hebrews 12:1 tell us to lay aside?","o":["Every weight and the sin that besets us","Our shoes","Our Bible","Our friends"],"why":"To run the race well."},{"q":"Who should we look to, according to Hebrews 12:2?","o":["Jesus","The coach","The crowd","Ourselves"],"why":"The author and finisher of our faith."},{"q":"What happened when Tobi dropped the backpack?","o":["He flew past half the runners","He fell over","He came last again","He went home"],"why":"Run free!"}]},"ry4s2":{"story":[{"sc":"college","n":"Exams were coming. Last term, Tobi had sat next to Femi, and Femi had shown him the answers. Tobi had promised God he'd never cheat again."},{"sc":"college","w":"rytobi","e":"smile","t":"I'll sit next to Femi again. I'm strong now. I won't look."},{"sc":"college","w":"ryle","e":"smirk","t":"Hmm. Do you put a bowl of hot puff-puff next to a hungry boy and say, 'Don't eat it'?"},{"sc":"college","w":"rytobi","e":"smile","t":"Ha! No, that would be asking for trouble."},{"sc":"college","w":"ryle","e":"big","t":"Rule two: don't just fight temptation. Run from it! Stay away from the places, people and things that make sin easy for you. It's not weakness. It's wisdom."},{"sc":"college","w":"ryle","e":"smile","t":"The Bible doesn't say 'walk past the path of the wicked and be strong'. It says: avoid it, pass not by it, turn from it, and pass away."},{"sc":"college","n":"Tobi asked to sit at the front of the hall for the exams. He scored lower than Femi. But he scored it honestly, and for the first time in a long while, he felt free."}],"quote":{"text":"Flee also youthful lusts: but follow righteousness, faith, charity, peace, with them that call on the Lord out of a pure heart.","who":"2 Timothy 2:22","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Don't play near the edge","text":"Tobi thought he was strong enough to sit next to temptation. Ryle's second rule: run from it. Avoid the places, people and things that make sin easy. That isn't weakness. It's wisdom."},"think":"What's one place, app or situation that makes it easy for you to do wrong? How could you avoid it?","quiz":[{"q":"What had Tobi promised God?","o":["Never to cheat again","To win every race","To play more","To skip exams"],"why":"Then he wanted to sit next to Femi."},{"q":"What did Ryle compare sitting next to Femi to?","o":["Putting hot puff-puff next to a hungry boy","A rainy day","A cricket match","A long walk"],"why":"Asking for trouble!"},{"q":"What was Ryle's second rule?","o":["Run from temptation","Be strong and stay near it","Never study","Always sit at the back"],"why":"Avoid what makes sin easy."},{"q":"What does 2 Timothy 2:22 say to do with youthful lusts?","o":["Flee","Follow","Ignore","Collect"],"why":"And follow righteousness."},{"q":"What does Proverbs 4:15 say to do with the path of evil?","o":["Avoid it, turn from it, and pass away","Walk along it carefully","Look at it","Build a house there"],"why":"Run!"}]},"ry4s3":{"story":[{"sc":"egyptcourt","w":"ryle","e":"smile","t":"Rule three: never forget that God's eye is on you, all the time, everywhere."},{"sc":"egyptcourt","n":"Long ago, a young man called Joseph was sold as a slave into Egypt. He worked hard in the house of an officer called Potiphar, and God blessed everything he did."},{"sc":"egyptcourt","n":"But Potiphar's wife kept trying to get Joseph to do something very wrong with her. Day after day she asked. And no one else was around to see."},{"sc":"egyptcourt","w":"ryjoseph","e":"stern","t":"How then can I do this great wickedness, and sin against God?"},{"sc":"egyptcourt","n":"One day she grabbed his coat. Joseph left the coat in her hand and ran out of the house! He was falsely accused and thrown into prison. But God was with him, and in the end, God raised him up to rule Egypt."},{"sc":"egyptcourt","w":"ryle","e":"big","t":"Notice what Joseph said: 'sin against God'. No one else was watching. But Joseph knew God was. That kept him safe."},{"sc":"egyptcourt","w":"ryle","e":"smile","t":"This isn't meant to frighten you. God's eye is the eye of a loving Father. He sees the wrong we're tempted to do, and he also sees every brave, hidden, good thing you do when no one else notices."},{"sc":"egyptcourt","w":"ryada","e":"smile","t":"So I'm never really alone. Not when I'm tempted, and not when I'm trying to do right."}],"quote":{"text":"How then can I do this great wickedness, and sin against God?","who":"Genesis 39:9","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Live before God's eyes","text":"Joseph was alone, but he knew God was watching, and he ran from sin. Ryle's third rule: remember God's eye is everywhere. It isn't to scare you; He's a loving Father who sees your hidden battles and your hidden kindness too."},"think":"How would you behave differently online and offline if you always remembered God is with you?","quiz":[{"q":"Where was Joseph sold as a slave?","o":["Egypt","Babylon","Rome","Nigeria"],"why":"To Potiphar's house."},{"q":"What did Joseph say when tempted?","o":["\"How can I sin against God?\"","\"Nobody's watching\"","\"Just this once\"","\"Maybe later\""],"why":"Genesis 39:9."},{"q":"What did Joseph leave behind when he ran?","o":["His coat","His sandals","His Bible","His staff"],"why":"He ran out of the house!"},{"q":"What was Ryle's third rule?","o":["Remember God's eye is always on you","Hide from God","Only behave when people watch","Never run"],"why":"A loving Father who sees."},{"q":"What does Proverbs 15:3 say the eyes of the LORD behold?","o":["The evil and the good","Only the good","Only the evil","Nothing"],"why":"In every place."}]},"ry4s4":{"story":[{"sc":"palace","w":"ryle","e":"smile","t":"Rule four, my last: pray. Pray in private, every day. And pray anywhere, at any moment."},{"sc":"palace","n":"Nehemiah was the {cupbearer} to the great King of Persia. One day the king noticed he looked sad, because Jerusalem's walls lay in ruins."},{"sc":"palace","w":"rynehemiah","e":"worried","t":"(The king is asking what I want. If I say the wrong thing, I could lose my life! Lord, help me...)"},{"sc":"palace","n":"The Bible says: 'So I prayed to the God of heaven. And I said unto the king...' A quick, silent prayer, in the middle of a conversation! And the king gave Nehemiah everything he needed to rebuild the walls."},{"sc":"study","w":"ryle","e":"smile","t":"Have a secret place where you pray every day, like Jesus taught. And between times, send quick prayers up all day long: before a test, during an argument, when you're scared."},{"sc":"study","n":"Ryle lived by this. He became the first Bishop of Liverpool in 1880, a busy city full of poor families. He worked hard there for twenty years, building churches, preaching and writing, and praying."},{"sc":"study","n":"In 1900, at the age of 84, he went home to be with the Lord. His plain, honest books are still read all over the world, including this one, written for you."},{"sc":"cricketfield","w":"ryle","e":"big","t":"So, young people: start now, watch out for the dangers, know Jesus, love His word, choose wise friends, drop sin, run from temptation, remember God sees, and pray. God bless you!"},{"sc":"cricketfield","w":"rytobi","e":"big","t":"Thank you, Bishop Ryle! We won't say 'later'. We'll start now."}],"quote":{"text":"So I prayed to the God of heaven. And I said unto the king...","who":"Nehemiah 2:4-5","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Pray in secret, pray anywhere","text":"Nehemiah sent up a quick prayer in front of the king. Ryle's last rule: have a secret place to pray every day, and pray anywhere, any time. Ryle lived this way all his life, and his words still reach young people today."},"think":"Where could your 'secret place' for prayer be? And when could you send up a quick prayer tomorrow?","quiz":[{"q":"What was Nehemiah's job?","o":["Cupbearer to the King of Persia","A farmer","A fisherman","A soldier"],"why":"A trusted servant."},{"q":"What did Nehemiah do before answering the king?","o":["Prayed a quick, silent prayer","Ran away","Asked a friend","Nothing"],"why":"So I prayed to the God of heaven."},{"q":"What did Jesus say to do when we pray?","o":["Enter your closet, shut the door, and pray in secret","Pray loudly on the street","Only pray in church","Never pray"],"why":"Matthew 6:6."},{"q":"How long did Ryle serve as Bishop of Liverpool?","o":["About twenty years","One week","Fifty years","He never did"],"why":"From 1880 to 1900."},{"q":"What did Tobi promise at the end?","o":["Not to say 'later', but start now","To play more cricket","To move to Liverpool","To stop reading"],"why":"Start now!"}]}}}});
